(text "POWER REVIEW: nominal 5 V / 500 mA architecture, inherited from the V3.0 approach.\nAt 14 V and 0.35 A the regulator dissipates about 3 W; thermal design is unresolved.\nThis protection circuit has not passed reverse battery, cranking, load dump or EMC testing.\nFuse, PTC and bulk-capacitor footprints remain blank pending exact part selection." (at 15 220 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 2c78df7c-e38a-5f74-b7ea-8e3ebbbd71cb))

(text "SUPPLY: vehicle 12 V through retained factory fused feeds; voltage regulation inside ECM. Existing onboard F1 is retained as a separate draft protection element. Retain factory fuse protection; input current budget and transient/reverse-polarity performance require validation." (at 15 270 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left top)) (uuid 6ba88277-0806-4984-a6eb-b4a22a7eb8fa))
